task.description:
TASK: Memory growth tied to utility — procedural/semantic memories don't time-decay, score-based selection, scaling budget

FILES TO MODIFY:

1. src/state/memory.ts — Three changes:

a) effectiveScore() — Only episodic memories should time-decay. Procedural and semantic knowledge is durable:
```ts
effectiveScore(m: Memory): number {
  const ageHours = (Date.now() - m.createdAt) / (1000 * 60 * 60);
  // Only episodic memories decay — procedural/semantic knowledge persists
  const decay = m.type === "episodic"
    ? Math.pow(0.5, ageHours / 24)
    : 1.0;
  const typeWeight = m.type === "procedural" ? 1.0 : m.type === "semantic" ? 0.85 : 0.5;
  const accessBoost = Math.log(1 + m.accessCount) * 0.15;
  return m.importance * typeWeight * decay + accessBoost;
}
```

b) formatAsMessages() — Select by score instead of chronological recency:
```ts
formatAsMessages(tokenBudget: number): MessagePair[] {
  // Select highest-scored memories that fit budget (not most recent)
  const ranked = [...this.memories]
    .sort((a, b) => this.effectiveScore(b) - this.effectiveScore(a));

  const selected: Memory[] = [];
  let totalTokens = 0;
  for (const m of ranked) {
    if (totalTokens + m.tokenCost > tokenBudget) continue;  // skip if too large, try next
    selected.push(m);
    totalTokens += m.tokenCost;
    m.accessCount++;  // track access for scoring boost
    m.lastAccessed = Date.now();
  }

  // Sort selected by creation time for conversation coherence
  selected.sort((a, b) => a.createdAt - b.createdAt);

  const messages: MessagePair[] = [];
  for (const m of selected) {
    messages.push({ role: "user", content: m.context || `[${m.type}]` });
    messages.push({ role: "assistant", content: m.content });
  }
  return messages;
}
```
Key: use `continue` not `break` — skip large memories but keep trying smaller ones.
Also: increment accessCount when memory is selected, creating the access boost feedback loop.

c) decayEvict() — Raise threshold or respect type:
```ts
decayEvict(threshold = 0.05): number {
  const before = this.memories.length;
  this.memories = this.memories.filter((m) => {
    // Never auto-evict procedural memories above minimum importance
    if (m.type === "procedural" && m.importance >= 0.3) return true;
    return this.effectiveScore(m) >= threshold;
  });
  return before - this.memories.length;
}
```

2. src/loop/state-machine.ts — Scale MEMORY_TOKEN_BUDGET with earned energy:
Change line 13 from:
```ts
const MEMORY_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4000;
```
to:
```ts
const BASE_MEMORY_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4000;
```

Then in the cycle() method (~line 184), compute dynamic budget:
```ts
const memoryBudget = BASE_MEMORY_TOKEN_BUDGET + Math.floor(this.state.energy.earned / 200);
const memoryMessages = this.state.memories.formatAsMessages(memoryBudget);
```
Agents that earn more get bigger memory budgets — compound interest.

Also update the MEMORY_TOKEN_BUDGET reference in finalizeCycle (~line 147) to use the same dynamic calculation.

After changes, run: npx tsc --noEmit
Commit with a clear message.
